# GPPS Procedure tables -- attachment / text-quality analysis
# + interactive JSON viewer  (FIXED VERSION)
#
# What changed from GPPS_Procedure_Analysis_Final.py:
#   The previous version measured "text length" using ONLY
#   procedureText.sgmntText. But procedures carry their real body
#   content the same way policies do -- in TWO places:
#     1. procedureText.sgmntText                      (short, top-level)
#     2. procedureApplication.segment[].procSgmntText (the actual body,
#        split across segments -- note the key is 'procSgmntText',
#        NOT 'sgmntText' like it is for policy segments)
#   Measuring only #1 was undercounting almost all of a procedure's
#   real content, which is the likely cause of the low "sufficient
#   text" numbers. This version combines both sources, the same way
#   the policy EDA combines policyText + policyApplication.segment[].
# ============================================================

